077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490127 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186489651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490127 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "59271587-d957-593c-984d-f14328120bc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490290 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490290 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160382" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490290 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490290 #edb/ref 1071 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{u}{v})\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  \n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490290 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "abc95782-56f0-5602-a797-77bbd8bc8d07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490290 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x=uv$ and $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{u}{v}).$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & u \\\\ \\frac{1}{u} & -\\frac{1}{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{v})-u\\cdot \\frac{1}{u} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,3)}=-2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490346 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490346 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "304d533c-c6df-5eb2-8572-8dad82b0c2ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490346 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490354 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5752fbe6-2298-595f-8f5f-87a185f8bc29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490354 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490360 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490360 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7925d591-5b75-52ac-b9d8-3ec5418695ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490360 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490373 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490373 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a74bfad6-ea65-5feb-a899-c8d57f2b8048" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490373 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186490290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490381 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186490354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490381 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c634b432-1616-5094-a080-a0dd00d9d507" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490381 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186389195 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
